  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-session-recycle-bin",
      "text": "**Session recycle bin & permanent delete for DeepSeek Harness.**\n\nMove the current session into a recycle bin from the conversation header, restore or permanently delete archived sessions (single or batch), with live-session protection.\n\nThe interface automatically follows the browser language: Chinese locales use\nChinese and all other locales use English.\n\n[English](README.md) | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "✨ Features",
      "text": "- **Conversation-header archive button** — move the current session into the recycle bin from the header (no confirmation; always recoverable).\n- **No duplicate of DSH's own affordance** — archiving from the sidebar uses DSH's built-in hover button; this plugin no longer injects a second, differently worded icon (0.4.4 removed the old row trash icon and the document-wide MutationObserver that drove it).\n- **Recycle-bin manager** (Settings → 🗑 会话回收站) — archived sessions with multi-select: batch restore, batch permanent delete; each item shows its ID and path.\n- **True permanent delete** — physically removes the session log from disk and the projection-cache record; ghost sessions (records without a log) are cleaned up so they vanish instead of lingering.\n- **Live-session protection** — sessions with an active agent are refused deletion.\n- **Sub-session aware** — each row can show how many sub-agent sessions it left behind (whole tree, any depth) and open them inline: title, size, time and running state, with a checkbox per sub-session. Permanent delete removes the whole tree; the ones you uncheck are kept and stay reachable as a \"deleted main session · N sub-sessions kept\" row inste"
    },
    {
      "section": "✨ Features",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "📋 Requirements",
      "text": "- **DSH 0.2.0-rc.2 or newer** (this release is tested on that version only; older hosts are untested)."
    },
    {
      "section": "📋 Requirements",
      "text": "The recycle-bin list no longer reads session logs: its titles and turn counts come from the Session projection cache (`SessionProjectionCache.cachedSnapshot`, plus `cachedPredecessorTitle` for checkpoints written by an older format generation) — the same zero-I/O face DSH's own session list uses. On a host without those two methods the plugin still mounts, archives and restores, but the list degrades to 「未命名会话」 with no turn counts."
    },
    {
      "section": "📋 Requirements",
      "text": "The floor is declared as `dsh.engines.dsh`. Note that DSH 0.2.0-rc.2 does **not** read that field: it is documentation for users and marketplaces, not a runtime gate.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "One-click from the plugin market (dsh-market)",
      "text": "Once listed in the [awesome-dsh-plugin](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com) registry: open **Settings → Plugin Market** → search **dsh-session-recycle-bin** → install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Manual",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-session-recycle-bin\n```\n\nThen restart the web app (stop the `dsh web` process and run `dsh web` again)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local development install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add link:/absolute/path/to/harness-session-delete\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-session-recycle-bin\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🚀 Usage",
      "text": "1. **Move to the recycle bin** — click the 「移入回收站」 icon in the conversation header: the session is archived and an undo toast appears. Whether an archived session keeps showing in the left sidebar is decided by DSH's own **View options → Filter sessions** setting (Hide archived / All conversations / Archived only); this plugin does not touch it, exactly like DSH's built-in archive button.\n2. **Settings recycle bin** — open **Settings ⚙️ → 🗑 会话回收站**:\n   - Checkbox multi-select → **Restore** (batch unarchive) or **Permanent delete** (batch purge).\n   - Each entry shows the session name, ID and working path (hover for full details).\n3. **Permanent delete** physically removes the log and projection cache; live sessions are protected.\n4. **Undo** — restoring shows an undo toast that re-archives the session."
    },
    {
      "section": "🚀 Usage",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🛠 Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm test          # run the test suite (host logic + HTTP routes)\n```\n\nRepo layout:\n\n```\nharness-session-delete/\n├── package.json            # single bundle manifest (dsh.bundle.patch + dsh.client)\n├── cordis.patch.yml        # bundle patch: one insert mounting the host row\n├── index.js                # node half: host entry (inject + apply)"
    },
    {
      "section": "🔌 How it works",
      "text": "- A **single npm bundle** covers both halves, same as other published plugins: the host row mounts via `cordis.patch.yml`; the browser half joins automatically through `dsh.client` + `exports[\"./client\"]`.\n- The browser talks to the host over the plugin's own `/api/session-trash/*` HTTP routes (registered on the webserver; non-GET requests carry an `x-dsh-plugin` CSRF header).\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "📄 License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
